- I can also create a one-page checklist you can bring to the appointment with the exact questions and space to fill in test results/recommendations.

Final note / safety
I can’t make medical decisions for you, but based on what you’ve given: your diabetes raises stroke risk by one point, age 55 does not automatically mandate anticoagulation, and many decisions hinge on other comorbidities, kidney function, symptom burden, and personal preferences. A brief visit with your PCP to get baseline tests and a clear CHA2DS2‑VASc/HAS‑BLED discussion will make the need for cardiology referral clear. If you’d like, tell me the clarifying details above and I’ll draft a tailored message to Dr. Lee or a checklist to take to the appointment. Which would you prefer?

