1) Key issues to clarify about AFib and anticoagulation
- Confirm diagnosis: ECG documentation (12‑lead) or prior Holter/monitor reports.
- Symptom status: symptomatic AF (palpitations, syncope, dyspnea) usually prompts more urgent/ specialized management.
- Type of AF: paroxysmal vs persistent vs permanent (affects monitoring and rhythm-control decisions).
- Stroke prevention: calculate CHA2DS2‑VASc to estimate stroke risk and decide on anticoagulation.
  - Points: congestive HF (1), hypertension (1), age ≥75 (2), age 65–74 (1), diabetes (1), stroke/TIA/thromboembolism (2), vascular disease (1), female sex (1).
