- Medications: calcium and vitamin D don’t greatly interact with DOACs. Warfarin has more dietary and drug interactions; long‑term warfarin has been associated with effects on bone metabolism in some studies (discuss if considering long-term warfarin).

When to refer to cardiology/EP now vs when PCP can manage
Refer now if any of:
- New or symptomatic AF (palpitations, syncope, recurring symptomatic episodes)
- Heart failure, structural or valvular disease suspected or known
- Prior stroke/TIA while in AF, or complex anticoagulation decision (high bleeding risk, renal disease)
